 r←Test_POSTRefresh_PendingRuns url;Assert;Authed;cache;file;state;tie
⍝ Check a refresh worker releases the lock and clears the pending flag, and that the
⍝ completed refresh leaves behind a cache file a later cold start could actually serve.
 r←0
 Assert←##.Assert
 Authed←##.MAIN.Authed
 state←#.DCMS.GLOBAL.refresh
 file←##.##.GetEnv'CACHE_FILE'
 :Trap 0
     'Refresh already running at start of test'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 150
    ⍝ Delete first, so the assertions below cannot be satisfied by a file an earlier run left
     :If ⎕NEXISTS file
         {}⎕NDELETE file
     :EndIf
     'Expected 202 Accepted'Assert 202=('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run.HttpStatus
     'Expected 202 Accepted'Assert 202=('POST'Authed url,'/admin/refresh').Run.HttpStatus
     'Refresh did not return to idle'Assert ##.WaitRefreshIdle 600
     'Pending flag not cleared'Assert 0=state.pending
     'Cache file not written'Assert ⎕NEXISTS file
     tie←file ⎕FTIE 0
     cache←⎕FREAD tie 1
     ⎕FUNTIE tie
     'Cache file does not hold a servable cache'Assert #.DCMS.CACHE.Valid cache
     r←1
 :EndTrap
⍝ Teardown: never leak a refresh worker, or a tie, into the next test
 {0::⍬ ⋄ ⎕FUNTIE tie}⍬
 {}##.WaitRefreshIdle 600
